~ start
Solaris: Mortal — the sun remembers when Agis bound us. I am the Warden of Rising Light.  
Solaris: Prove that your mind burns as brightly as your courage.
[do! get_tree().get_first_node_in_group("player").lock_player()]
[do! DialogueManager.solaris.face_player()]
=> Q1

~ Q1
Solaris: According to the Even–Odd identities — what is sin(-x)?
- A. sin(-x) = sin(x) => Q1_WRONG
- B. sin(-x) = -sin(x) => Q1_CORRECT
- C. sin(-x) = cos(x) => Q1_WRONG
- D. sin(-x) = -cos(x) => Q1_WRONG

~ Q1_CORRECT
Solaris: Bold and right. The flame favors truth. [do! DialogueManager.solaris.trigger_correct_answer()]
=> Q2

~ Q1_WRONG
Solaris: Your answer is as cold as shadow. [do! DialogueManager.solaris.trigger_wrong_answer()]
=> END

~ Q2
Solaris: What is the general solution for sin(θ) = 0?
- A. θ = n·π => Q2_CORRECT
- B. θ = 2·n·π => Q2_WRONG
- C. θ = π/2 + n·π => Q2_WRONG
- D. θ = π/2 + 2·n·π => Q2_WRONG

~ Q2_CORRECT
Solaris: Correct. The pattern reveals itself. [do! DialogueManager.solaris.trigger_correct_answer()]
=> Q3

~ Q2_WRONG
Solaris: No — that is not general enough. [do! DialogueManager.solaris.trigger_wrong_answer()]
=> END

~ Q3
Solaris: If cos(θ) = −1 and 0 ≤ θ < 2π, what is θ?
- A. 0 => Q3_WRONG
- B. π/2 => Q3_WRONG
- C. π => Q3_CORRECT
- D. 2π => Q3_WRONG

~ Q3_CORRECT
Solaris: Well answered — the orbit is precise. [do! DialogueManager.solaris.trigger_correct_answer()]
=> Q4

~ Q3_WRONG
Solaris: You misplace the angle. [do! DialogueManager.solaris.trigger_wrong_answer()]
=> END

~ Q4
Solaris: The principal value of arcsin(0.5) is:
- A. 120° => Q4_WRONG
- B. 30° => Q4_CORRECT
- C. 150° => Q4_WRONG
- D. 210° => Q4_WRONG

~ Q4_CORRECT
Solaris: Sharp. Your sight is true. [do! DialogueManager.solaris.trigger_correct_answer()]
=> Q5

~ Q4_WRONG
Solaris: Incorrect — think on the unit circle. [do! DialogueManager.solaris.trigger_wrong_answer()]
=> END

~ Q5
Solaris: Which identity is commonly used to solve trig equations?
- A. sin²(θ) + cos²(θ) = 1 => Q5_CORRECT
- B. sin(θ) = adjacent/hypotenuse => Q5_WRONG
- C. tan(θ) = hypotenuse/opposite => Q5_WRONG
- D. sec(θ) = 1/tan(θ) => Q5_WRONG

~ Q5_CORRECT
Solaris: The light approves. You have passed my trial. [do! DialogueManager.solaris.trigger_death()]
[do! get_tree().get_first_node_in_group("player").unlock_player()]
[do! DialogueManager.solaris.queue_free()]
=> END!

~ Q5_WRONG
Solaris: You falter — be gone! [do! DialogueManager.solaris.trigger_wrong_answer()]
=> END